window.docContents[227].resolve({"/UD-V___-encapsulation/Objects/#Core-C______--UD-V___-encapsulation--Objects":{"contents":"The expression new C(args) allocates one location per field of the whole chain of , the root base first, then the tagged record, and runs the constructors from the root base down, each with this bound to the object, the one of  with the arguments and the others with none, since there are no initialiser lists. A class without a constructor is created by new C() and keeps the default values.\n\nThe call of a member body, a method, a constructor or a destructor, binds this to the location  of the receiver as an alias and the parameters as in the call of a function, by value with a fresh copy and by reference with an alias. The return frees the copies and the locals of the body, never the receiver.With  in place of  the result is  for a void member and error otherwise.\n\nA method call e.m(args) needs a receiver of class type and e->m(args) a receiver of pointer type. The method is the nearest  in the chain of the static class of the receiver, it must be visible, and the arguments are checked as in a call. An unqualified call m(args) inside a member body is this->m(args).\n\n","context":"Core C++\u0009UD V, encapsulation","header":"6.2. Objects","id":"/UD-V___-encapsulation/Objects/#Core-C______--UD-V___-encapsulation--Objects"}});